/-!
# The left ideals of high-order currents in a level enveloping algebra

Let `ĝ = L((t)) ⊕ R K` be the residue central extension of an invariant symmetric form `Φ`, and let
`U = U(ĝ) / (ι K - a)` be its enveloping algebra at the central value `a`
(`TauCeti.UniversalEnvelopingAlgebra.CentralQuotient`), generated by the currents
`LieAlgebra.ofTwoCocycle.envelopingι c a u` for the residue cocycle `c` of `Φ`. For an integer
`N`, this file studies the left ideal

`I_N = U · ι(a_N)`

generated by the currents of order at least `N`, that is by `L ⊗ tᴺ R[[t]]`
(`TauCeti.CurrentAlgebra.orderLeftIdeal`). It is a submodule of the left regular `U`-module, not
a two-sided ideal, so `Q_N = U / I_N` is a left `U`-module and not a quotient ring. The ideals
decrease as `N` grows, so for `M ≥ N` there is the transition map `Q_M → Q_N`, which is
`Submodule.factor (orderLeftIdeal_antitone _ _ _ _ h)`.

The main result is the right-shift estimate
`TauCeti.CurrentAlgebra.exists_forall_mul_mem_orderLeftIdeal`: for every `b ∈ U` and every `N`
there is `M` with `I_M b ⊆ I_N`. For a current generator `u` of order at least `p` and a current
`v` of order at least `M`, the commutator relation gives

`v u = u v + ⁅v, u⁆ + a Res(v du)`,

where `⁅v, u⁆` has order at least `M + p` and the residue term vanishes once `M + p > 0`; so
`M = max N (max (N - p) (1 - p))` works for `b = u`. The general case follows because the set of
`b` admitting such estimates is a subalgebra, and the current generators generate `U`. No
finiteness of `L` and no completeness are used.

Consequently each `Q_N` is smooth for the family `I`, in the sense of `TauCeti.smoothModules`
(`TauCeti.CurrentAlgebra.smoothModules_quotient_orderLeftIdeal`), and smoothness for `I` is the
same as smoothness of the current action: every vector is killed by the currents of some order
(`TauCeti.CurrentAlgebra.smoothModules_orderLeftIdeal_iff`). These quotients are the stages of the
completed enveloping algebra `lim_N U / I_N`.

Algebra morphisms between such enveloping algebras which carry the high-order currents into the
corresponding left ideal carry the whole left ideal there
(`TauCeti.CurrentAlgebra.orderLeftIdeal_le_comap`). In particular the level comparison
`TauCeti.CurrentAlgebra.levelEnvelopingEquiv` matches the left ideals of the two levels
(`TauCeti.CurrentAlgebra.levelEnvelopingEquiv_mem_orderLeftIdeal_iff`), for every level including
zero.

Over a field the left ideals separate: `⋂_N I_N = 0`
(`TauCeti.CurrentAlgebra.iInf_orderLeftIdeal`), for every value of `a`, including `a = 0`, and
without any finiteness of `L`. So `U` embeds in the limit of the modules `U / I_N`. For `n ≥ 0` the
pairs `(u, z)` with `u` of order at least `n` form a Lie subalgebra `a_n ⊕ K K` of `ĝ`, on which
`(u, z) ↦ a z` is a character because the residue cocycle vanishes on currents of nonnegative
order. The preimage of `I_n` in `U(ĝ)` is the left ideal induced from this character. These
subalgebras decrease to `K K`, so by the Poincaré--Birkhoff--Witt theorem for induced modules
(`TauCeti.UniversalEnvelopingAlgebra.iInf_span_range_ι_sub_algebraMap`) the preimages intersect in
the left ideal generated by `ι K - a`, which is the kernel of `U(ĝ) → U`.

The same induced-module PBW theorem gives the exact degree-one relations at nonnegative
order: `ι(u) - b ∈ I_N` if and only if `u ∈ a_N` and `b = 0`. In particular, every such
`I_N` is proper, including at central value zero.

For `n = 0` the negative currents `t⁻¹ L[t⁻¹]` (`TauCeti.CurrentAlgebra.negativeLieSubalgebra`)
form a Lie subalgebra of `ĝ` complementing `L[[t]] ⊕ R K`, so the same theorem for induced modules
describes `U / I₀`: over any commutative ring, every element of `U` is congruent modulo `I₀` to the
image of an element of `U(t⁻¹ L[t⁻¹])`
(`TauCeti.CurrentAlgebra.exists_sub_negativeEnvelopingHom_mem_orderLeftIdeal`), and over a field a
nonzero element of `U(t⁻¹ L[t⁻¹])` never maps into `I₀`
(`TauCeti.CurrentAlgebra.negativeEnvelopingHom_mem_orderLeftIdeal_iff`). In particular
`U(t⁻¹ L[t⁻¹])` embeds in `U`, for every value of `a`.

## Main definitions

* `TauCeti.CurrentAlgebra.orderLeftIdeal`: the left ideal `I_N` generated by the currents of order
  at least `N`.

## Main results

* `TauCeti.CurrentAlgebra.orderLeftIdeal_antitone`: the left ideals decrease.
* `TauCeti.CurrentAlgebra.iInf_orderLeftIdeal_natCast`: the left ideals of natural orders have the
  same intersection as all of them.
* `TauCeti.CurrentAlgebra.exists_forall_mul_mem_orderLeftIdeal`: the right-shift estimate
  `∀ b N, ∃ M, I_M b ⊆ I_N`.
* `TauCeti.CurrentAlgebra.smoothModules_orderLeftIdeal_iff`: smoothness for the family `I_N` is
  smoothness of the current action.
* `TauCeti.CurrentAlgebra.smoothModules_orderLeftIdeal_natCast`: smoothness for the `I_n` of
  natural orders is smoothness for all the `I_N`.
* `TauCeti.CurrentAlgebra.smoothModules_quotient_orderLeftIdeal`: each `U / I_N` is smooth.
* `TauCeti.CurrentAlgebra.levelEnvelopingEquiv_mem_orderLeftIdeal_iff`: the level comparison
  matches the left ideals.
* `TauCeti.CurrentAlgebra.iInf_orderLeftIdeal`: over a field, `⋂_N I_N = 0`.
* `TauCeti.CurrentAlgebra.envelopingι_sub_algebraMap_mem_orderLeftIdeal_iff`: the degree-one
  relations in a congruence quotient at nonnegative order.
* `TauCeti.CurrentAlgebra.orderLeftIdeal_ne_top`: these congruence quotients are nonzero.
* `TauCeti.CurrentAlgebra.exists_sub_negativeEnvelopingHom_mem_orderLeftIdeal`: `U / I₀` is
  generated over `U(t⁻¹ L[t⁻¹])` by the class of `1`.
* `TauCeti.CurrentAlgebra.negativeEnvelopingHom_mem_orderLeftIdeal_iff`: over a field, it is a
  free `U(t⁻¹ L[t⁻¹])`-module of rank one on the class of `1`.

## References

* E. Frenkel, *Langlands Correspondence for Loop Groups*, §2.1.2 and §3.2.1, for the left ideals
  generated by `𝔤 ⊗ tᴺ ℂ[[t]]`, the completion `lim_N U / I_N` of the enveloping algebra of an
  affine Kac--Moody algebra at a fixed level, and the smoothness of the quotients `U / I_N`.
-/

public section

noncomputable section

open scoped LaurentSeries
open LieAlgebra TauCeti.UniversalEnvelopingAlgebra
open LieAlgebra.ofTwoCocycle (centralElement ofProd_symm_centralElement centralElement_mem_center
  envelopingι envelopingι_apply ι_ofProd envelopingι_mul_sub_mul adjoin_range_envelopingι)

attribute [local instance 1100] HahnSeries.instAlgebra
attribute [local instance 100] LieRing.ofAssociativeRing

namespace TauCeti.CurrentAlgebra

universe v

variable {R L : Type*} [CommRing R] [LieRing L] [LieAlgebra R L]

local notation "C" => currentAlgebra R L

section LeftIdeal

variable (Φ : LinearMap.BilinForm R L) (hΦ : Φ.lieInvariant L) (hΦs : Φ.IsSymm) (a : R)

local notation "c" => twoCocycleOfBilinear R L Φ hΦ hΦs
local notation "UK" => CentralQuotient R (centralElement c) a

/-- The left ideal `I_N` of `U(ĝ) / (ι K - a)` generated by the currents of order at least `N`,
as a submodule of the left regular module. -/
def orderLeftIdeal (N : ℤ) : Submodule UK UK :=
  Submodule.span UK (envelopingι c a '' orderSubmodule R L N)

/-- The left ideal `I_N` is spanned by the current generators of order at least `N`. -/
theorem orderLeftIdeal_def (N : ℤ) : orderLeftIdeal Φ hΦ hΦs a N =
    Submodule.span UK (envelopingι c a '' orderSubmodule R L N) :=
  (rfl)

variable {Φ hΦ hΦs a}

/-- The current generator of a current of order at least `N` lies in `I_N`. -/
theorem envelopingι_mem_orderLeftIdeal {N : ℤ} {u : C} (hu : u ∈ orderSubmodule R L N) :
    envelopingι c a u ∈ orderLeftIdeal Φ hΦ hΦs a N :=
  Submodule.subset_span ⟨u, hu, rfl⟩

/-- `I_N` is contained in a left ideal exactly when the currents of order at least `N` are. -/
theorem orderLeftIdeal_le_iff {N : ℤ} {I : Submodule UK UK} :
    orderLeftIdeal Φ hΦ hΦs a N ≤ I ↔ ∀ u ∈ orderSubmodule R L N, envelopingι c a u ∈ I := by
  rw [orderLeftIdeal_def, Submodule.span_le, Set.image_subset_iff]
  rfl

variable (Φ hΦ hΦs a)

/-- The left ideals `I_N` decrease as `N` grows. -/
theorem orderLeftIdeal_antitone : Antitone (orderLeftIdeal Φ hΦ hΦs a) := fun _ _ h ↦
  orderLeftIdeal_le_iff.2 fun _ hu ↦
    envelopingι_mem_orderLeftIdeal (orderSubmodule_antitone R L h hu)

/-- The left ideals `I_n` of natural orders `n` decrease as `n` grows. -/
theorem orderLeftIdeal_natCast_antitone :
    Antitone fun n : ℕ ↦ orderLeftIdeal Φ hΦ hΦs a n :=
  (orderLeftIdeal_antitone Φ hΦ hΦs a).comp_monotone Nat.mono_cast

/-- The left ideals `I_n` of natural orders `n` have the same intersection as all the left ideals
`I_N`, since the natural numbers are cofinal among the orders. -/
theorem iInf_orderLeftIdeal_natCast :
    ⨅ n : ℕ, orderLeftIdeal Φ hΦ hΦs a n = ⨅ N : ℤ, orderLeftIdeal Φ hΦ hΦs a N := by
  refine le_antisymm (le_iInf fun N ↦ ?_) (le_iInf fun n ↦ iInf_le _ _)
  exact (iInf_le _ N.toNat).trans (orderLeftIdeal_antitone Φ hΦ hΦs a (Int.self_le_toNat N))

variable {Φ hΦ hΦs a}

/-- The product of the current generators of a current `v` of order at least `M` and a current `u`
of order at least `p`, in this order, lies in `I_N` when `N ≤ M`, `N ≤ M + p` and `0 < M + p`. -/
theorem envelopingι_mul_envelopingι_mem_orderLeftIdeal {M N p : ℤ} {u v : C}
    (hv : v ∈ orderSubmodule R L M) (hu : u ∈ orderSubmodule R L p) (hNM : N ≤ M)
    (hNp : N ≤ M + p) (hp : 0 < M + p) :
    envelopingι c a v * envelopingι c a u ∈ orderLeftIdeal Φ hΦ hΦs a N := by
  rw [← sub_add_cancel (envelopingι c a v * _) (envelopingι c a u * _),
    envelopingι_mul_sub_mul, twoCocycleOfBilinear_coe, twoCochainOfBilinear_apply_apply,
    LinearEquiv.apply_symm_apply, residuePairing_eq_zero_of_mem_orderSubmodule R L Φ hv hu hp,
    mul_zero, map_zero, add_zero]
  refine add_mem (envelopingι_mem_orderLeftIdeal ?_) ?_
  · exact orderSubmodule_antitone R L hNp (lie_mem_orderSubmodule R L hv hu)
  · exact (orderLeftIdeal Φ hΦ hΦs a N).smul_mem _
      (envelopingι_mem_orderLeftIdeal (orderSubmodule_antitone R L hNM hv))

variable (Φ hΦ hΦs a) in
/-- **The right-shift estimate.** For every `b ∈ U(ĝ) / (ι K - a)` and every `N` there is `M` with
`I_M b ⊆ I_N`. -/
theorem exists_forall_mul_mem_orderLeftIdeal (b : UK) (N : ℤ) :
    ∃ M : ℤ, ∀ x ∈ orderLeftIdeal Φ hΦ hΦs a M, x * b ∈ orderLeftIdeal Φ hΦ hΦs a N := by
  refine exists_forall_mul_mem_of_adjoin_eq_top (orderLeftIdeal_antitone Φ hΦ hΦs a).directed_ge
    (adjoin_range_envelopingι c a) ?_ b N
  rintro _ ⟨u, rfl⟩ N
  obtain ⟨p, hu⟩ := exists_mem_orderSubmodule R L u
  refine ⟨max N (max (N - p) (1 - p)), fun x hx ↦ ?_⟩
  -- The elements whose right multiple by `u` lies in `I_N` form a left ideal.
  refine (orderLeftIdeal_le_iff (I := (orderLeftIdeal Φ hΦ hΦs a N).comap
    (LinearMap.toSpanSingleton UK UK (envelopingι c a u)))).2 (fun v hv ↦ ?_) hx
  exact envelopingι_mul_envelopingι_mem_orderLeftIdeal hv hu (by omega) (by omega) (by omega)

variable (Φ hΦ hΦs a) in
/-- The right-shift estimate for the left ideals `I_n` of natural orders: for every `b` and `n`
there is a natural `m` with `I_m b ⊆ I_n`. -/
theorem exists_forall_mul_mem_orderLeftIdeal_natCast (b : UK) (n : ℕ) :
    ∃ m : ℕ, ∀ x ∈ orderLeftIdeal Φ hΦ hΦs a m, x * b ∈ orderLeftIdeal Φ hΦ hΦs a n := by
  obtain ⟨M, hM⟩ := exists_forall_mul_mem_orderLeftIdeal Φ hΦ hΦs a b n
  exact ⟨M.toNat, fun x hx ↦ hM x (orderLeftIdeal_antitone Φ hΦ hΦs a (Int.self_le_toNat M) hx)⟩

/-- **Smoothness for `I_N` is smoothness of the current action.** A module over
`U(ĝ) / (ι K - a)` is smooth for the family of left ideals `I_N` exactly when every vector is
killed by all currents of some order. -/
theorem smoothModules_orderLeftIdeal_iff {M : ModuleCat.{v} UK} :
    smoothModules (orderLeftIdeal Φ hΦ hΦs a) M ↔
      ∀ m : M, ∃ N : ℤ, ∀ u ∈ orderSubmodule R L N, envelopingι c a u • m = 0 := by
  rw [smoothModules_iff]
  refine forall_congr' fun m ↦ exists_congr fun N ↦ ⟨fun h u hu ↦
    h _ (envelopingι_mem_orderLeftIdeal hu), fun h x hx ↦ ?_⟩
  -- The annihilator of `m` is a left ideal containing the currents of order at least `N`.
  have hle : orderLeftIdeal Φ hΦ hΦs a N ≤ LinearMap.ker (LinearMap.toSpanSingleton UK M m) :=
    orderLeftIdeal_le_iff.2 h
  exact hle hx

variable (Φ hΦ hΦs a) in
/-- Smoothness for the left ideals `I_n` of natural orders is smoothness for all the left ideals
`I_N`, since the natural numbers are cofinal among the orders. -/
theorem smoothModules_orderLeftIdeal_natCast :
    smoothModules.{v} (fun n : ℕ ↦ orderLeftIdeal Φ hΦ hΦs a n) =
      smoothModules (orderLeftIdeal Φ hΦ hΦs a) :=
  le_antisymm (smoothModules_le_of_forall_exists_le fun n ↦ ⟨n, le_rfl⟩)
    (smoothModules_le_of_forall_exists_le fun N ↦
      ⟨N.toNat, orderLeftIdeal_antitone Φ hΦ hΦs a (Int.self_le_toNat N)⟩)

variable (Φ hΦ hΦs a) in
/-- **Each quotient `U / I_N` is smooth** for the family of left ideals `I_M`: the class of `b` is
killed by `I_M` whenever `I_M b ⊆ I_N`. -/
theorem smoothModules_quotient_orderLeftIdeal (N : ℤ) :
    smoothModules (orderLeftIdeal Φ hΦ hΦs a)
      (ModuleCat.of UK (UK ⧸ orderLeftIdeal Φ hΦ hΦs a N)) := by
  refine smoothModules_iff.2 fun m ↦ ?_
  obtain ⟨b, rfl⟩ := Submodule.Quotient.mk_surjective _ m
  obtain ⟨M, hM⟩ := exists_forall_mul_mem_orderLeftIdeal Φ hΦ hΦs a b N
  refine ⟨M, fun x hx ↦ ?_⟩
  rw [← Submodule.Quotient.mk_smul, smul_eq_mul, Submodule.Quotient.mk_eq_zero]
  exact hM x hx

end LeftIdeal

section Induced

variable (Φ : LinearMap.BilinForm R L) (hΦ : Φ.lieInvariant L) (hΦs : Φ.IsSymm) (a : R)

local notation "c" => twoCocycleOfBilinear R L Φ hΦ hΦs
local notation "E" => ofTwoCocycle c
local notation "UE" => UniversalEnvelopingAlgebra R E
local notation "mkR" => CentralQuotient.mk (centralElement c) a

/-- Membership of `(u, z)` in `orderExtensionLieSubalgebra` only constrains the current
coordinate. -/
private theorem ofProd_mem_orderExtensionLieSubalgebra {n : ℕ} {u : currentAlgebra R L}
    {z : TrivialLieModule R (currentAlgebra R L) R} :
    ofProd c (u, z) ∈ orderExtensionLieSubalgebra Φ hΦ hΦs n ↔ u ∈ orderSubmodule R L n := by
  simp

/-- The quotient map sends the relation `ι(u, z) - a z` to the current generator of `u`. -/
private theorem mk_ι_sub_centralCoordinateForm_ofProd (u : currentAlgebra R L)
    (z : TrivialLieModule R (currentAlgebra R L) R) :
    mkR (UniversalEnvelopingAlgebra.ι R (ofProd c (u, z)) -
      algebraMap R UE (centralCoordinateForm Φ hΦ hΦs a (ofProd c (u, z)))) =
        envelopingι c a u := by
  rw [map_sub, AlgHom.commutes, ← CentralQuotient.ι_apply, ι_ofProd,
    centralCoordinateForm_ofProd, add_sub_cancel_right]

/-- The left ideal of `U(ĝ)` generated by the elements `ι x - a z` for `x = (u, z)` with `u` of
order at least `n`. -/
private def inducedLeftIdeal (n : ℕ) : Submodule UE UE :=
  Submodule.span UE (Set.range fun x : orderExtensionLieSubalgebra Φ hΦ hΦs n ↦
    UniversalEnvelopingAlgebra.ι R (x : E) -
      algebraMap R UE (centralCoordinateForm Φ hΦ hΦs a x))

/-- The preimage of `I_n` in `U(ĝ)` lies in the induced left ideal: `I_n` is the image of the
induced left ideal, which contains the kernel `U(ĝ) (ι K - a)` of the quotient map. -/
private theorem mem_inducedLeftIdeal_of_mk_mem {n : ℕ} {w : UE}
    (hw : mkR w ∈ orderLeftIdeal Φ hΦ hΦs a n) : w ∈ inducedLeftIdeal Φ hΦ hΦs a n := by
  have hI : orderLeftIdeal Φ hΦ hΦs a n ≤ Ideal.map mkR (inducedLeftIdeal Φ hΦ hΦs a n) := by
    refine orderLeftIdeal_le_iff.2 fun u hu ↦ ?_
    have hmem : UniversalEnvelopingAlgebra.ι R (ofProd c (u, 0)) -
        algebraMap R _ (centralCoordinateForm Φ hΦ hΦs a (ofProd c (u, 0))) ∈
          inducedLeftIdeal Φ hΦ hΦs a n :=
      Submodule.subset_span ⟨⟨_, (ofProd_mem_orderExtensionLieSubalgebra Φ hΦ hΦs).2 hu⟩, rfl⟩
    simpa only [mk_ι_sub_centralCoordinateForm_ofProd] using Ideal.mem_map_of_mem mkR hmem
  obtain ⟨w', hw', hmk⟩ := (Ideal.mem_map_iff_of_surjective mkR
    (CentralQuotient.mk_surjective _ a)).1 (hI hw)
  obtain ⟨y, hy⟩ := (CentralQuotient.mk_eq_mk_iff a (centralElement_mem_center c)
    (u := w) (v := w')).1 hmk.symm
  have hK := centralElement_mem_orderExtensionLieSubalgebra Φ hΦ hΦs n
  have hrel : y * (UniversalEnvelopingAlgebra.ι R (centralElement c) - algebraMap R UE a) ∈
      inducedLeftIdeal Φ hΦ hΦs a n := by
    refine Submodule.smul_mem _ y (Submodule.subset_span ⟨⟨_, hK⟩, ?_⟩)
    simp
  rw [← hy] at hrel
  simpa using add_mem hw' hrel

/-- The image of the induced left ideal in `U(ĝ) / (ι K - a)` lies in `I_n`: the relation
`ι(u, z) - a z` maps to the current generator of `u`. -/
private theorem mk_mem_orderLeftIdeal_of_mem_inducedLeftIdeal {n : ℕ} {w : UE}
    (hw : w ∈ inducedLeftIdeal Φ hΦ hΦs a n) : mkR w ∈ orderLeftIdeal Φ hΦ hΦs a n := by
  have hle : inducedLeftIdeal Φ hΦ hΦs a n ≤ Ideal.comap mkR (orderLeftIdeal Φ hΦ hΦs a n) := by
    refine Submodule.span_le.2 ?_
    rintro _ ⟨⟨x, hx⟩, rfl⟩
    obtain ⟨⟨u, z⟩, rfl⟩ := (ofProd c).surjective x
    rw [ofProd_mem_orderExtensionLieSubalgebra] at hx
    rw [SetLike.mem_coe, Ideal.mem_comap, mk_ι_sub_centralCoordinateForm_ofProd]
    exact envelopingι_mem_orderLeftIdeal hx
  exact hle hw

/-- The negative currents are a complement of the subalgebra `L[[t]] ⊕ R K` inducing `I₀`. -/
private theorem isCompl_negativeLieSubalgebra :
    IsCompl (negativeLieSubalgebra Φ hΦ hΦs : Submodule R E)
      (orderExtensionLieSubalgebra Φ hΦ hΦs 0 : Submodule R E) := by
  have h := isCompl_truncSubmodule_orderSubmodule R L 0
  refine ⟨Submodule.disjoint_def.mpr fun x hx hx' ↦ ?_,
    codisjoint_iff.mpr (eq_top_iff.mpr fun x _ ↦ ?_)⟩
  · obtain ⟨⟨u, z⟩, rfl⟩ := (ofProd c).surjective x
    rw [LieSubalgebra.mem_toSubmodule, ofProd_mem_negativeLieSubalgebra] at hx
    rw [LieSubalgebra.mem_toSubmodule, ofProd_mem_orderExtensionLieSubalgebra, Nat.cast_zero]
      at hx'
    obtain ⟨hu, rfl⟩ := hx
    rw [Submodule.disjoint_def.mp h.disjoint u hu hx', Prod.mk_zero_zero, of_zero]
  · obtain ⟨⟨u, z⟩, rfl⟩ := (ofProd c).surjective x
    obtain ⟨p, hp, q, hq, rfl⟩ := Submodule.mem_sup.mp (h.sup_eq_top ▸ Submodule.mem_top (x := u))
    have hpq : ((p + q, z) : currentAlgebra R L × _) = (p, 0) + (q, z) := by simp
    rw [hpq, of_add]
    refine Submodule.add_mem_sup ?_ ?_
    · simpa using hp
    · simpa [ofProd_mem_orderExtensionLieSubalgebra] using hq

/-- The left ideal induced from the character `orderCharacter` at order zero is
`inducedLeftIdeal`. -/
private theorem span_orderCharacter :
    Submodule.span UE (Set.range fun x : orderExtensionLieSubalgebra Φ hΦ hΦs 0 ↦
      UniversalEnvelopingAlgebra.ι R (x : E) -
        algebraMap R UE (orderCharacter Φ hΦ hΦs a 0 x)) =
        inducedLeftIdeal Φ hΦ hΦs a 0 := by
  simp only [orderCharacter_apply, centralCoordinateForm_apply, inducedLeftIdeal]

/-- **The negative currents span modulo `I₀`.** Over any commutative ring, every element of
`U(ĝ) / (ι K - a)` is congruent modulo `I₀` to the image of an element of the enveloping algebra
of the negative currents `t⁻¹ L[t⁻¹]`. -/
theorem exists_sub_negativeEnvelopingHom_mem_orderLeftIdeal
    (u : CentralQuotient R (centralElement c) a) :
    ∃ y, u - negativeEnvelopingHom Φ hΦ hΦs a y ∈ orderLeftIdeal Φ hΦ hΦs a 0 := by
  obtain ⟨w, rfl⟩ := CentralQuotient.mk_surjective _ a u
  obtain ⟨y, hy⟩ := exists_sub_map_mem_span_range_ι_sub_algebraMap (orderCharacter Φ hΦ hΦs a 0)
    (isCompl_negativeLieSubalgebra Φ hΦ hΦs).sup_eq_top w
  rw [span_orderCharacter] at hy
  refine ⟨y, ?_⟩
  simpa [negativeEnvelopingHom_apply] using
    mk_mem_orderLeftIdeal_of_mem_inducedLeftIdeal Φ hΦ hΦs a hy

end Induced

section Separation

variable {K : Type*} [Field K] [LieAlgebra K L]
  (Φ : LinearMap.BilinForm K L) (hΦ : Φ.lieInvariant L) (hΦs : Φ.IsSymm) (a : K)

local notation "cK" => twoCocycleOfBilinear K L Φ hΦ hΦs
local notation "EK" => ofTwoCocycle cK
local notation "UE" => UniversalEnvelopingAlgebra K EK
local notation "mkK" => CentralQuotient.mk (centralElement cK) a

/-- **The degree-one relations of a congruence quotient.** At nonnegative order, a current
generator minus a scalar belongs to `I_N` exactly when the current has order at least `N`
and the scalar is zero. In particular there are no additional degree-one relations caused
by the central-level quotient. -/
@[simp]
theorem envelopingι_sub_algebraMap_mem_orderLeftIdeal_iff {N : ℤ} (hN : 0 ≤ N)
    (u : currentAlgebra K L) (b : K) :
    envelopingι cK a u - algebraMap K _ b ∈ orderLeftIdeal Φ hΦ hΦs a N ↔
      u ∈ orderSubmodule K L N ∧ b = 0 := by
  refine ⟨fun hw ↦ ?_, fun ⟨hu, hb⟩ ↦ by
    simpa [hb] using envelopingι_mem_orderLeftIdeal (Φ := Φ) (hΦ := hΦ) (hΦs := hΦs)
      (a := a) hu⟩
  let n := N.toNat
  have hn : (n : ℤ) = N := Int.toNat_of_nonneg hN
  let B := orderExtensionLieSubalgebra Φ hΦ hΦs n
  let χ : LieCharacter K B :=
    { toLinearMap := (centralCoordinateForm Φ hΦ hΦs a).comp B.incl.toLinearMap
      map_lie' := fun {x y} ↦ by
        simpa only [LinearMap.toFun_eq_coe, LinearMap.comp_apply, LieHom.coe_toLinearMap,
          LieSubalgebra.coe_incl, LieSubalgebra.coe_bracket,
          LieRing.of_associative_ring_bracket, mul_comm, sub_self] using
          centralCoordinateForm_lie_eq_zero Φ hΦ hΦs a n x x.property y y.property }
  have hw' : UniversalEnvelopingAlgebra.ι K (ofProd cK (u, 0)) - algebraMap K UE b ∈
      inducedLeftIdeal Φ hΦ hΦs a n := by
    apply mem_inducedLeftIdeal_of_mk_mem Φ hΦ hΦs a
    simpa [hn, envelopingι_apply, CentralQuotient.ι_apply] using hw
  obtain ⟨v, hv, hb⟩ :=
    (ι_sub_algebraMap_mem_span_range_ι_sub_algebraMap_iff χ).mp hw'
  have hu : u ∈ orderSubmodule K L n :=
    by simpa using (show ofProd cK (u, 0) ∈
      orderExtensionLieSubalgebra Φ hΦ hΦs n from hv ▸ v.property)
  have hb' : centralCoordinateForm Φ hΦ hΦs a (v : EK) = b := hb
  rw [hv, centralCoordinateForm_ofProd] at hb'
  exact ⟨hn ▸ hu, by simpa using hb'.symm⟩

/-- A current generator vanishes in the congruence quotient exactly at the prescribed order. -/
@[simp]
theorem envelopingι_mem_orderLeftIdeal_iff {N : ℤ} (hN : 0 ≤ N)
    (u : currentAlgebra K L) :
    envelopingι cK a u ∈ orderLeftIdeal Φ hΦ hΦs a N ↔
      u ∈ orderSubmodule K L N := by
  simpa using envelopingι_sub_algebraMap_mem_orderLeftIdeal_iff Φ hΦ hΦs a hN u 0

/-- Congruence quotients at nonnegative order are nonzero, at every central value. -/
theorem orderLeftIdeal_ne_top {N : ℤ} (hN : 0 ≤ N) :
    orderLeftIdeal Φ hΦ hΦs a N ≠ ⊤ := by
  intro h
  have hw : envelopingι cK a 0 - algebraMap K _ 1 ∈
      orderLeftIdeal Φ hΦ hΦs a N := h ▸ Submodule.mem_top
  exact one_ne_zero
    ((envelopingι_sub_algebraMap_mem_orderLeftIdeal_iff Φ hΦ hΦs a hN 0 1).mp hw).2

/-- The quotient map kills the relations of the intersection of the
  `orderExtensionLieSubalgebra`, which
consists of the multiples of the central element. -/
private theorem span_iInf_orderExtensionLieSubalgebra_le_comap :
    Submodule.span UE (Set.range fun x : ↥(⨅ n, orderExtensionLieSubalgebra Φ hΦ hΦs n) ↦
      UniversalEnvelopingAlgebra.ι K (x : EK) - algebraMap K UE (centralCoordinateForm Φ hΦ hΦs a
        x)) ≤
        Ideal.comap mkK ⊥ := by
  refine Submodule.span_le.2 ?_
  rintro _ ⟨⟨x, hx⟩, rfl⟩
  obtain ⟨⟨u, z⟩, rfl⟩ := (ofProd cK).surjective x
  have hu : u = 0 := by
    rw [← Submodule.mem_bot K, ← iInf_orderSubmodule K L, Submodule.mem_iInf]
    intro N
    have h : u ∈ orderSubmodule K L N.toNat := by
      simpa using iInf_le (orderExtensionLieSubalgebra Φ hΦ hΦs) N.toNat hx
    exact orderSubmodule_antitone K L (Int.self_le_toNat N) h
  subst hu
  rw [SetLike.mem_coe, Ideal.mem_comap, Ideal.mem_bot, map_sub, AlgHom.commutes,
    ← CentralQuotient.ι_apply, ι_ofProd, map_zero, zero_add, centralCoordinateForm_ofProd, sub_self]

/-- **PBW separation of the left ideals `I_N`.** Over a field, the left ideals `I_N` of
`U(ĝ) / (ι K - a)` generated by the currents of order at least `N` intersect in zero, for every
central value `a`, including `a = 0`. Thus `U(ĝ) / (ι K - a)` embeds in the inverse limit of the
left modules `U / I_N`. -/
@[simp]
theorem iInf_orderLeftIdeal : ⨅ N, orderLeftIdeal Φ hΦ hΦs a N = ⊥ := by
  rw [eq_bot_iff]
  intro x hx
  obtain ⟨x, rfl⟩ := CentralQuotient.mk_surjective _ a x
  -- A lift of `x` lies in every induced left ideal, hence in the one induced from their
  -- intersection, which the quotient map kills.
  have hxJ : x ∈ ⨅ n, inducedLeftIdeal Φ hΦ hΦs a n := (Submodule.mem_iInf _).2 fun n ↦
    mem_inducedLeftIdeal_of_mk_mem Φ hΦ hΦs a ((Submodule.mem_iInf _).1 hx n)
  unfold inducedLeftIdeal at hxJ
  rw [UniversalEnvelopingAlgebra.iInf_span_range_ι_sub_algebraMap
    (orderExtensionLieSubalgebra_antitone Φ hΦ hΦs).directed_ge _
    (centralCoordinateForm_lie_eq_zero Φ hΦ hΦs a)]
    at hxJ
  simpa using span_iInf_orderExtensionLieSubalgebra_le_comap Φ hΦ hΦs a hxJ

/-- **The negative currents act freely modulo `I₀`.** Over a field, the image of an element `y`
of the enveloping algebra of the negative currents `t⁻¹ L[t⁻¹]` lies in `I₀` only if `y = 0`. -/
@[simp]
theorem negativeEnvelopingHom_mem_orderLeftIdeal_iff
    {y : UniversalEnvelopingAlgebra K (negativeLieSubalgebra Φ hΦ hΦs)} :
    negativeEnvelopingHom Φ hΦ hΦs a y ∈ orderLeftIdeal Φ hΦ hΦs a 0 ↔ y = 0 := by
  refine ⟨fun hy ↦ ?_, fun hy ↦ by simp [hy]⟩
  have h := mem_inducedLeftIdeal_of_mk_mem Φ hΦ hΦs a (n := 0)
    (w := map K (negativeLieSubalgebra Φ hΦ hΦs).incl y)
    (by simpa [negativeEnvelopingHom_apply] using hy)
  rw [← span_orderCharacter] at h
  exact (map_mem_span_range_ι_sub_algebraMap_iff_of_isCompl (orderCharacter Φ hΦ hΦs a 0)
    (isCompl_negativeLieSubalgebra Φ hΦ hΦs)).1 h

/-- Over a field, the enveloping algebra of the negative currents `t⁻¹ L[t⁻¹]` embeds in
`U(ĝ) / (ι K - a)`, for every central value `a`. -/
theorem negativeEnvelopingHom_injective : Function.Injective (negativeEnvelopingHom Φ hΦ hΦs a) :=
  (injective_iff_map_eq_zero _).2 fun y hy ↦ by
    rw [← negativeEnvelopingHom_mem_orderLeftIdeal_iff Φ hΦ hΦs a, hy]
    exact zero_mem _

end Separation

section Map

variable {Φ Ψ : LinearMap.BilinForm R L} {hΦ : Φ.lieInvariant L} {hΦs : Φ.IsSymm}
  {hΨ : Ψ.lieInvariant L} {hΨs : Ψ.IsSymm} {a b : R}

local notation "cΦ" => twoCocycleOfBilinear R L Φ hΦ hΦs
local notation "cΨ" => twoCocycleOfBilinear R L Ψ hΨ hΨs

/-- An algebra morphism which carries the currents of order at least `N` into `I_N'` carries the
whole left ideal `I_N` into `I_N'`. -/
theorem orderLeftIdeal_le_comap
    {g : CentralQuotient R (centralElement cΨ) b →ₐ[R]
      CentralQuotient R (centralElement cΦ) a} {N N' : ℤ}
    (hg : ∀ u ∈ orderSubmodule R L N,
      g (envelopingι cΨ b u) ∈ orderLeftIdeal Φ hΦ hΦs a N') :
    orderLeftIdeal Ψ hΨ hΨs b N ≤ Ideal.comap g (orderLeftIdeal Φ hΦ hΦs a N') :=
  orderLeftIdeal_le_iff.2 hg

/-- **The level comparison matches the left ideals.** If `Ψ = k • Φ`, the isomorphism
`levelEnvelopingEquiv` from `U(ĝ_Ψ) / (ι K - 1)` to `U(ĝ_Φ) / (ι K - k)` carries each `I_N` onto
`I_N`, for every `k`, including `k = 0`. -/
@[simp]
theorem levelEnvelopingEquiv_mem_orderLeftIdeal_iff {k : R} (h : Ψ = k • Φ) {N : ℤ}
    {x : CentralQuotient R (centralElement cΨ) 1} :
    levelEnvelopingEquiv hΦ hΦs hΨ hΨs h x ∈ orderLeftIdeal Φ hΦ hΦs k N ↔
      x ∈ orderLeftIdeal Ψ hΨ hΨs 1 N := by
  let e := levelEnvelopingEquiv hΦ hΦs hΨ hΨs h
  refine ⟨fun hx ↦ ?_, fun hx ↦ orderLeftIdeal_le_comap (g := e.toAlgHom) (fun u hu ↦ ?_) hx⟩
  · simpa [e] using orderLeftIdeal_le_comap (g := e.symm.toAlgHom)
      (fun u hu ↦ by simpa [e] using envelopingι_mem_orderLeftIdeal hu) hx
  · simpa [e] using envelopingι_mem_orderLeftIdeal hu

end Map

end TauCeti.CurrentAlgebra
